    "title": "Form field identity lookup",
    "role": "guide",
    "authority": "markdown_source"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# Form field identity lookup\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "Form field identity lookup"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "PDF writing builds a local ordered index of source object-number/generation\npairs once, then resolves each existing form field through that index. Reordered\nfields retain their original object identities without rescanning every PDF\nfield for every document field. Duplicate references retain first-match behavior.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 7,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 8,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "The original-name fallback remains a live search because renaming a field or a\nparent can change fully-qualified names during the same write. It is not cached\nusing stale names. The index is private to one write and does not survive a PDF\nmutation or hold references across documents.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000006",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 12,
      "end_line": 12,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 13,
      "end_line": 15,
      "raw": "`PdfFormLookupTest` creates an independent xref-table PDF with 256 fields, reverses\nthe document field order, exercises missing-source name fallback, renames all\nfields and verifies that all original values and identities survive a round trip.\n"
    }
  ],
